### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hardware Heterogeneity** | CPU performance is highly dependent on memory bandwidth (single vs. quad channel), which affects the comparison. | Disclose exact RAM frequency and channel configuration. |
| **Software/Driver Overhead** | Vulkan and CUDA have different driver/runtime overheads that may skew small-batch results. | Report "Warm-up" runs and include driver/toolkit versions. |
| **Resource Contention** | Running 8 threads on CPU might starve the OS/background tasks, whereas GPU offloading leaves CPU free. | Use a process affinity mask to isolate CPU cores and monitor background CPU load. |
| **Output Non-Determinism** (Workload) | If the prompt or temperature settings differ, the "workload" (number of tokens generated/paths taken) changes. | **Control:** Use a fixed seed and identical prompt/max-token settings across all three backends. |

